00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.120
episode

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.120
"Minuet

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.120
of the Unrequited"

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.420
Thank you, André.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.050
Sure.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.850
It's already been 2 years since
the war of independence ended.

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.520
Everyone returned soon afterwards,
so what were you doing? And where?

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.470
I'm sorry for making you worry.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.560
Right as I was about to return,
I came down with a febrile illness,

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.570
so I stayed behind in America alone.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:38.440
In and out of bed... My recovery
took longer than I had expected.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.070
I see...

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.810
It's delicious!

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:48.040
It's been so long since I've
had real French cooking.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.820
I've really come back to France, haven't I?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.120
It's starting to sink in...

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.000
<i>Oscar.</i>

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.840
<i>There's only one thing I can do now.</i>

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.300
<i>I choose to be a coward in Her Majesty's eyes!</i>

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.630
<i>I'm going to run away.</i>

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:08.600
<i>I must!</i>

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.560
<i>To a far off place, thousands of
miles away across the ocean!</i>

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.970
<i>Oscar, please take care of Lady Antoinette!</i>

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.110
I'm really glad you returned safely.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:32.090
Lady Oscar, I've prepared a bed in the
second floor guest room for Lord Fersen.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.040
No, you shouldn't have, Oscar.
I'll go back to my manor.

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:37.900
I'll send someone to your manor
tomorrow with a message that says,

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.730
''The Jarjayes will provide the Count with relaxing
accommodations to ease his travel fatigue.''

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:45.010
A week, a month... Stay as long as you like.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.300
Oscar...

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.460
Please do, then.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.000
After all, it's been 7 years.

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:52.540
I'd like to catch up with you, as well.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.980
And hear your stories about America.

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.320
Thank you.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.320
I'm surrounded by such wonderful friends...

00:04:59.320 --> 00:04:59.990
Thank you.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:05.460
I was willing to abandon everything, even my life,
when I went to the battlefield, but...

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.950
I'm happy to be alive...

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.130
Let's have another toast.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:14.870
To Count Fersen's return from this
several thousand mile journey!

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.170
Let's.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:16.830
Cheers!

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.000
Cheers!

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:19.960
Thank you.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.360
You're up so early. Did you sleep well, Fersen?

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.850
Ah, yes. Very well.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:50.070
Getting up early is a battlefield habit.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:51.300
Old habits die hard.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.000
I see, as long you slept.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:57.880
You should visit her and report
your return as soon as possible.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.540
I'm sure Her Majesty is worried about you, as well.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.550
I know I should eventually, but...

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:05.970
I intend to return to Sweden without seeing her.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:11.420
Seven years ago, I ran away from Lady Antoinette.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.950
It was a selfish and cowardly decision.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.150
And so, it ended...

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.690
It was for the better that our love ended.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:25.400
The only reason I returned to France
was to reaffirm that for myself.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:28.450
That I no longer burn with love... To know that
my love will never burn like that again...

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.510
I've decided to take you up on your offer and
stay for another week or two at your manor.

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.420
I realized if I go back to my manor,
word would spread that I've returned.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:41.990
Please, Oscar.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:45.220
Please don't tell Her Majesty that I've returned.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:47.220
All right...

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:10.530
Come on, André!

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.250
Pass me if you can!

00:07:20.090 --> 00:07:22.460
<i>I never expected this...</i>

00:07:22.460 --> 00:07:26.090
<i>Lady Antoinette is no longer in Fersen's heart.</i>

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:28.060
<i>Could that really be possible though?</i>

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.150
<i>But if...</i>

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:31.720
<i>If that's truly the case...</i>

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.220
<i>Fersen, the man right before me now,</i>

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.690
<i>is the one and only man
I've felt that I could love.</i>

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.400
<i>Hans Axel von Fersen...</i>

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.620
Come to think of it, Oscar...

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.990
I hear you've been promoted to Brigadier...

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.320
...for your outstanding work
in the necklace incident.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.960
Your nanny told me this morning.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.630
Ah, yes...

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:54.890
Congratulations!

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:58.240
If it were up to me, I would have
promoted you all the way up to General.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:02.990
It's nothing short of a mystery
that God made you a woman.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.890
André, are you all right?! Are you hurt?!

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.110
No, I'm all right.

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.390
Such a heinous act!

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:26.310
Who were they?!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.730
Harassers from Paris, most likely.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.030
Paris citizens?! But why?

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.460
It's been happening a lot lately.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:34.470
I hear other nobles' manors
have been targeted, as well.

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:35.830
Ever since the necklace incident,

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:38.990
the number of people who resent the
nobility and royal family has grown rapidly.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:43.960
In fact, some nobles have even cut their ties with
the royal family to join hands with the people.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:45.980
That's inconceivable...!

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.600
I vaguely heard the rumors, but still...

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.980
During the 7 years you've been gone, Paris, Versailles...

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:54.590
...and all of France have been slowly changing.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:56.190
How though?

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:57.430
What kind of changes?

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.440
The age of the nobility will soon come to an end.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:09.400
We no longer believe the royal
family is France, herself.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:14.110
If we have to eat lousy food, the Queen and her
circle should have to eat lousy food, as well!

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:15.220
That's right!

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.520
Why should they be the only
ones eating good food?!

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.290
That's our tax money!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.090
That's right!

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:24.040
If they eat good food, we should also be able to!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.850
That's right!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:32.190
Yesterday, a child died in the Gravilliers district.

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.330
The child died because he couldn't buy bread.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.780
Two days ago, a woman died
in the Temple district.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:45.900
The woman died because she worked
too hard to provide milk to her child.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:46.680
Die!

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.860
Fat pigs should all die!

00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:04.190
It's changed...

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.580
France has indeed changed...

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:12.460
Back then, there were some who spoke ill,
but the royal family was still loved...

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:16.130
Her Majesty was still loved by her people...

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:30.780
Oscar, I've decided to go to Versailles, after all.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.930
The royal family is now facing a crisis.

00:10:35.930 --> 00:10:38.200
The only thing I can do at such a time...

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.830
The only thing I can do for my love
who I can't forget, although I've tried...

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:44.990
...is to be by her side.

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:50.250
No matter what anyone says,

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:53.130
I can't idly watch misfortune
befall the woman I love!

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:08.980
Thank goodness...
Thank goodness you're safe...

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.200
I, too, am glad to see Your Majesty is well.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.810
Oscar.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:24.910
It's time for target practice. Are you coming?

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:25.980
Yeah.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:27.220
I'm coming.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:28.650
Wait for me downstairs.

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:29.450
Okay!

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:55.690
There!

00:12:09.860 --> 00:12:14.460
A new movement has an intensity
that is similar to a raging fire.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:17.460
I learned this first hand,
during my time in America.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.920
There are several small fires that have
begun to burn in France, as well.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.890
Before its embers reach the royal family,
these fires must be extinguished.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:30.550
If you would allow me,

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:34.810
I am ready to serve by Your Majesty's
side for the rest of my life.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:38.690
After 7 years, I have learned...

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:42.430
...the foolishness of letting one's heart burn
passionately, and the dangers it brings.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.320
I will not let it burn so intensely again.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.530
Instead, like the eternal flow of the Seine,

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:51.910
I will keep my feelings for
you lit in my heart forever.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.200
Like the flow of the Seine...

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:55.670
Yes.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.350
Look, Oscar.

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:09.590
Migrating birds.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:11.350
They're heading back south.

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:16.480
They're free to fly the limitless skies,
yet they always return to the same place.

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:18.980
No one can stop them.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:20.650
No one...

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:28.970
Your Majesty.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:32.960
I must offer my opinion as your loyal servant.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.920
Please leave this villa and return
to the Palace of Versailles.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:38.880
Due to Your Majesty's move here,

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:42.420
I hear a number of nobles' hearts have become
estranged from the royal family.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:46.720
Please return to Versailles and call
back those nobles immediately.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.970
It's imperative that you keep at least
the nobles on your side now.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:53.550
Furthermore, please cut your ties with
Madame Polignac and her circle.

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:57.940
If the Queen only listens to the opinions of
her inner circle and only grants their requests,

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:02.070
it will be a source of resentment among
the nobles at court, including the people.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.780
In exchange, I, Hans Axel von Fersen,

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:10.140
will abandon my homeland, Sweden.

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:12.870
For Your Majesty's sake...

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.700
I will devote my all to France.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:35.970
Have you heard, Madame Eloff?

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.910
Yes, about Her Majesty.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.710
I hear she's leaving the villa and returning
to the Palace of Versailles.

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:43.110
I wonder why the sudden change of heart?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.120
I wonder?

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:47.280
Also, have you heard about Madame Polignac?

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.590
My, I wonder what could it be?

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:51.720
Remember how the post for Minister
of Finance has yet to be filled?

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:52.360
Yes.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.830
Well, Madame Polignac requested
Her Majesty to appoint...

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.030
...one of her relatives as the new Minister.

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:00.430
My, like she always does.

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:04.000
Yes, but Her Majesty said this to her:

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:07.910
''I've decided that I shouldn't decide
such matters solely at my discretion.''

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:11.640
''Please make your request to
His Majesty through proper channels.''

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:12.270
My...!

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:18.270
I hear Madame Polignac and her circle's
influence are growing weaker by the day.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.860
That aside, we have good reason to be happy.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:26.820
Today, Lady Antoinette will finally leave
the villa and return to Versailles.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.390
She'll also resume her audiences
with the nobles, among other duties.

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:35.240
She probably took heed of
Count Fersen's suggestions.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:39.570
The Count is now officially a reserve
Colonel of the Army Regiment,

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.710
and reports for duty at the
Palace of Versailles every day.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.970
Have a good day.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:54.220
Everyone, take three steps forward!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.520
In a short while, our squad...

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.190
...will guard and escort Her Majesty from
the Trianon villa to the Palace of Versailles.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:05.730
Furthermore, if you see anything odd
while escorting her, report it immediately.

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.600
Hold your positions until I give the orders.

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.290
All right, take your positions!

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:34.680
Die nobles!!

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:38.390
Take your emergency positions!

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:51.180
An assailant is escaping!

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.150
Capture him!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:39.450
V... Vive la France...

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.270
Pull yourself together, Oscar!

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.920
What are you thinking about at a time like this?!

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.080
Oscar.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.210
What's wrong?

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:00.370
Are you injured?

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:04.780
André, tell Girodelle to take charge of the rest.

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.040
I'm going home.

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.940
Oscar...

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.330
<i>Fersen...</i>

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:15.880
<i>Ah, Fersen...</i>

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:19.490
<i>You returned to the person
who needs you the most</i>

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:22.690
<i>and also loves you the most.</i>

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:25.370
<i>After 7 years of separation,</i>

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.400
<i>7 years of agony,</i>

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.340
<i>you still went back to her.</i>

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:33.150
<i>I think you've done a wonderful thing.</i>

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:36.210
<i>I think you're a wonderful person.</i>

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.280
With all my heart...

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:42.180
For the first time as a woman, I...

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:53.300
Where's that corset?

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:55.130
Ah, the pannier, the pannier!

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.830
Um, the stockings are...

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:59.070
What's going on, Grandma?

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:03.410
All that dressmaking and my
persistence have finally paid off!

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:04.990
A dress...?

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:09.710
Lady Oscar said she's going
to wear it to tonight's ball.

00:19:10.350 --> 00:19:11.020
What?!

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.170
Oscar is going to wear a dress?!

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:15.790
D-Don't tighten it so hard!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:16.750
You'll split me in half!

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.590
Please stay still!

00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:19.820
O-Ow...!

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.060
Are you trying to rip my scalp off?!

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.090
I'm trying to do an updo!

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.690
There are things called hairstyles!

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.070
<i>Have you lost your mind, Oscar?</i>

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:34.480
<i>My Oscar is going to wear a flashy dress and dance with men?!</i>

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.040
Please, Oscar in a dress?

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:39.180
She'll look like a tall scarecrow
with fabric thrown over it.

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:40.370
It'll be unsightly!

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:42.240
André!

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:43.710
Come here!

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:44.520
Okay, okay.

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:45.120
Coming!

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:46.350
André!

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:47.580
All right, all right.

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:50.590
Have a look at our Lady in a dress!

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:51.450
Sure, sure.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:07.570
My, Madame!

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:08.440
Look over there!

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:09.700
My...!

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:12.190
Who is she?

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.980
She looks as though a Greek
statue has come alive.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.380
I hear she's a Countess from a foreign country.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:19.880
Her name is being kept secret,
due to her high rank.

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.580
My, from a foreign country?

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:36.380
I've seen her somewhere...

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:41.800
Madame.

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:46.930
May I have the next dance, please?

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:55.490
My, she moves so gracefully.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.390
She has such a slender figure, too.

00:20:57.390 --> 00:20:59.730
Even Lord Fersen is enchanted by her.

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:06.060
Countess, which country have you come from?

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:10.490
I know someone who looks very much like you.

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:14.540
She's also very beautiful and has blonde hair.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:17.210
She's kindhearted and is highly educated, as well.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:19.500
She'd throw her life away for her convictions!

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:23.590
She normally covers her fragrant skin
in a gold braided military uniform,

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:26.480
and rejects the gazes of men like an icy flower.

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.520
She's my most precious
and beautiful friend.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:42.860
Please forgive me.

00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:47.320
Could you possibly be...?!

00:21:50.810 --> 00:21:52.210
Could you possibly be...?!

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:12.200
<i>Fersen's arms embraced me...</i>

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:16.720
<i>Fersen's eyes surrounded me
and his lips spoke of me...</i>

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:19.570
<i>I can give it all up now...</i>

00:22:19.570 --> 00:22:21.150
<i>Now I can finally give it all up!</i>

